\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, Thou fount of every blessing,
\par Tune my heart to sing Thy grace;
\par Streams of mercy never ceasing
\par Call for songs of loudest praise.
\par Teach me some melodious measure
\par Sung by flaming tongues above;
\par O the vast, the boundless treasure
\par Of my Lord's unchanging love!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Here I raise my Ebenezer;
\par Hither by Thy help I'm come;
\par And I hope, by Thy good pleasure,
\par Safely to arrive at home.
\par Jesus sought me when a stranger,
\par Wandering from the fold of God;
\par He, to rescue me from danger,
\par Interposed His precious blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O to grace how great a debtor
\par Daily I'm constrained to be!
\par Let that grace, Lord, like a fetter,
\par Bind my wandering heart to Thee:
\par Prone to wander, Lord, I feel it.
\par Prone to leave the God I love;
\par Take my heart, O take and seal it,
\par Seal it from Thy courts above!
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

